# Uncorrelated IN and NOT IN subqueries inside a condition (ADR 0041's SQ7, its first PR): under OR, NOT and CASE WHEN
# in WHERE, an inner ON (inside a FULL JOIN's left input too) and HAVING, and in the CASE WHEN of a select item, an ORDER
# BY item, a GROUP BY key and an aggregate's argument, in plain, grouped and global blocks and inside derived tables,
# CTEs and subquery blocks. Each is a null-aware mark join: TRUE on a match; FALSE over an empty set, even for a NULL
# probe; else NULL where the probe is NULL or the set holds a NULL; else FALSE. NOT IN is NOT over it. A top-level
# conjunct keeps its semi or null-aware anti join, and so does an IN that every branch of an OR shares.

# ---- WHERE and ON ----

