# Three-valued marks under OR and NOT. A set with a NULL makes a NOT IN never true, so only the other branch keeps rows;
# the empty set makes NOT IN true and IN false; a set of NULLs only makes IN NULL. Over edge, whose i32 is NULL at ids 5
# and 9: the set of ids 2, 3 and 5 holds 0, -1 and a NULL and matches ids 2 and 3; a set without a NULL keeps NULL
# probes out of a NOT IN, the empty set keeps them in; a CASE picks the rows whose IN is NULL (every row but the match,
# over a set with a NULL) and FALSE (over a set without one); NOT over an IN of a set with a NULL is never true; NOT
# over an OR drops the NULL probe of id 5.

